t;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1249958" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/infra/suite_scheduler" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/infra/suite_scheduler" ref="refs/changes/58/1249958/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I2bc824b5e787369fdae1f6e40961722ddd7c1adb" commit="a2447ce7679e0a7778e3cc4547aee0c5cf67c5e0" commit_message="CHROMIUM: media: ipu3-imgu: Convert macros in structs to enum  Address comments from v6 upstream: Link: https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/10316733/  BUG=b:116082248 TEST=Sanity checked camera functions  Fixes: commit c30916e8a517 (&quot;CHROMIUM: media: ipu3-imgu: Synchronize the code with FROMLIST v6&quot;) Change-Id: I2bc824b5e787369fdae1f6e40961722ddd7c1adb Signed-off-by: Yong Zhi &lt;yong.zhi@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1241535 Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1241535" owner_email="yong.zhi@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/35/1241535/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="I0ba0152111b45dda7a20b766f9a5126452530a5e" commit="14e3c429220d78cf83f51af2c75cf23944245b8e" commit_message="FROMGIT: drm/msm/dpu: Remove dpu_mdss_isr when dpu_mdss_destroy is called  The MDSS device is created before the MSM driver attempts to bind the sub components. If any of the components return -EPROBE_DEFER the MDSS device is destroyed and tried again later.  If this happens the dpu_mdss_isr interrupt created from the DPU MDSS is not freed when the MDSS device is destroyed and has a risk of triggering later and hitting a fault by accessing a mmio region that no longer exists. Even if the interrupt isn't triggered by accident when the device attempts to reprobe it would error out when it tries to re-register the interrupt so unconditionally removing it in the destroy is the right move.  Switch the device managed dpu_mdss_isr to be unmanaged and add a free_irq() in the mdss destroy function.  Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Jordan Crouse &lt;jcrouse@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt;  (cherry picked from commit dd6e81c48f83d062058f4c66745d8b2c9f5c5458) (am from git://people.freedesktop.org/~robclark/linux) Signed-off-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=None TEST=Tested on cheza  Change-Id: I0ba0152111b45dda7a20b766f9a5126452530a5e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1228238 Commit-Ready: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1228238" owner_email="seanpaul@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/38/1228238/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id42cb39ef398367d2492ea989e278713484ee4ab" commit="e6a0aa3cf05f4f53a7834ab177b494432fc7f872" commit_message="tast-tests: Make screenshot package use color.Color.  Remove the screenshot package's Color struct and make it instead use the existing color.Color interface (and color.NRGBA behind the scenes for non-alpha-premultiplied, 8-bit-per-channel RGBA colors).  Also simplify some code for getting an image's dimensions.  BUG=chromium:888262 TEST=verified that graphics.Screenshot passes on sumo and      vm.CrostiniStartEverything passes on banon  Change-Id: Id42cb39ef398367d2492ea989e278713484ee4ab Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1255459 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Teste